# --- Kept on disk, kept out of the published repository -----------------------
# These stay in the working tree because they are still useful locally. They are
# not published: they describe the private cloud original this was ported from,
# carry absolute paths from the machine that wrote them, or are screenshots of
# real data. Adding a pattern here does NOT untrack a file that git already
# knows about — `git rm -r --cached <path>` is what removes it from the index.

# Internal working documents
/checkpoint.md
/docs/MIGRATION-PLAN.md
/docs/DELTAS.md
/docs/RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md
/docs/superpowers/

# Verification records: receipts, run results, screenshots. The reusable harness
# out of this tree now lives in apps/desktop/test/ and apps/backend/test/agent-cli/.
/docs/receipts/

# Better Auth docs inherited from the cloud original — the desktop port has no
# auth stack — plus the compiled .js/.d.ts/.map artifacts committed beside them.
/apps/backend/docs/

# Temporal search-attribute helper. Temporal is gone from the desktop port.
/apps/backend/scripts/

# Unmodified NestJS and Vite template READMEs.
/apps/backend/README.md
/apps/frontend/README.md
.gstack/
